Hi there,

I am running a CFA using the following code:

library(lavaan)
model <- "
  f1 =~ item_1 + item_2 + item_3 + item_5 + item_6 + item_8
"
fit <- lavaan::cfa(model, data = df, estimator = "MLR", std.lv <http://std.lv> = T)

My df has around 350 observations, with around 330 who completed all of these items. Those who did not completed none of the items.

When I inspect the results using summary(fit), it works well (see full results at the bottom of the post).

However, when I want to inspect the modification indices, using modindices = T in the summary function, I get no results:

Modification Indices:

[1] lhs      op       rhs      mi       epc      sepc.lv <http://sepc.lv>  sepc.all sepc.nox
<0 rows> (or 0-length row.names)

When I call modindices(fit), it gives me a df with 0 observations of 8 variables.

I found in a previous post <https://groups.google.com/g/lavaan/c/wcsBewKpPPI> that this can occur when your model is fully saturated, and you have df = 0. However, that is not the case, as I have df = 9. Moreover, inspection of the correlation residuals shows there should be plenty modifications that could improve model fit (see figure at bottom of post).

I do not have this problem when fitting a different model (2 factors, around 12 items per factor) to the same df (using different items). Using ML estimation instead of MLR, or std.lv <http://std.lv> = F instead of std.lv <http://std.lv> = T does not solve the issue.

Does anyone know what's going wrong?

With kind regards,
Jop Flameling

