You can have many endogenous categorical (ordinal) variables. Frequently, most or all observed variables are only ordinal, and lavaan churns right through that. I suspect that you "solved the problem" in passing. That is, the actual solution may have been accidentally achieved while trying to impose a different "solution."449 iterations for a path model seems like a lot, even with two groups, so I'm not sure that you have entirely dealt with the issue. If you want to look forther, I strongly suggest breaking your model down into pieces, and figuring out which pieces run well and which do not.

